  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A uniform wire of length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L\"></span> is made of copper. What is the relationship between the wire’s radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span>, the wire’s resistance <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span>, and the wire’s resistivity <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\rho\"></span>?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\\: \\alpha\\: \\sqrt{\\frac{\\rho}{R}}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\\: \\alpha\\: \\sqrt{\\frac{R}{\\rho}}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\\: \\alpha\\: \\frac{\\rho}{R}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\\: \\alpha\\: \\frac{R}{\\rho}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
